From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wings Build <wings@example.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 02:35:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] cccs: increase post-update swap timeout

On NAND/TrustFence systems, update-firmware may need several seconds to
update the redundant U-Boot environment. CCCS runs the active-system swap
synchronously after an on-the-fly SWU and previously allowed only two
seconds, causing DRM to report a failed update even when the swap command
completed successfully from the shell.

Increase only this post-update swap command timeout to 30 seconds.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [product-specific timeout for NAND/TrustFence]

---
 library/src/cc_firmware_update.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/library/src/cc_firmware_update.c b/library/src/cc_firmware_update.c
--- a/library/src/cc_firmware_update.c
+++ b/library/src/cc_firmware_update.c
@@ -1467,7 +1467,7 @@ static void firmware_reset_cb(unsigned int const target, ccapi_bool_t *system_reset
 		log_fw_debug("%s", "On-the-fly update finished. Now we will reboot the system");
 
 		/* Swap the active system partition */
-		if (ldx_process_execute_cmd("update-firmware --swap-active-system --no-reboot", &resp, 2) != 0) {
+		if (ldx_process_execute_cmd("update-firmware --swap-active-system --no-reboot", &resp, 30) != 0) {
 			if (resp != NULL)
 				log_fw_error("Error swapping active system: %s", resp);
 			else
-- 
